DEBUG sendPayload result {"whatsappId":"919176719261@s.whatsapp.net","result":{"key":{"remoteJid":"919176719261@s.whatsapp.net","fromMe":true,"id":"3EB0553977FDDFBD263509"},"message":{"extendedTextMessage":{"text":"Namaskaram,\nWe kindly request your attention to the following ashram policies and guidelines.\n\nPlease carefully review the important information below and reply to confirm your understanding and agreement.\nWe will only be able to proceed with your volunteering application after receiving your confirmation.\n\nImportant Guidelines:\nFocus and Purpose\nIt is vital to maintain focus on the purpose of your visit to the Sadhguru Sannidhi, refraining from forming personal relationships or friendships.\n\nConduct\nAs the ashram maintains a monastic environment, we kindly request that public displays of affection, including those among married couples, be avoided.\n\nAttire\nDuring day to day activities, it is required to wear traditional Indian clothing. Clothing should be non-revealing and cover the shoulders and midriff. Pants should be ankle length.\n\nDaily Schedule\nDuring your stay you will be expected to follow a specific schedule, starting at 4.45 am and ending by 9.30 pm.\n\nActive Participation\nVolunteers are expected to engage in various activities while at the SadhguruSannidhi, which may involve both office-based and physical volunteering activities.\n\nSeva Attendance\nDaily attendance for volunteering activities is mandatory. Volunteers are expected to arrive on time and mark their attendance at each activity.\n\nMedical Treatment\nThose who fall ill while staying at the Sadhguru Sannidhi will be required to follow any advice given by the medical team, which may include taking allopathic medicines and may involve hospitalization in more serious cases. Failure to follow the medical instructions will result in immediate discontinuation of stay.\n\nFinancial Preparedness\nIt is essential to have sufficient funds for your visit, including provisions for any unforeseen medical emergencies. In the case of emergency hospitalization, you will be required to pay for the hospital treatment, as well as any essential expenses required for a hospital attendant provided by the ashram (food, transportation, etc.).\n\nAshram Coordination\nContinuation of stay will be granted on the basis of following these guidelines. Failure to adhere to the ashram guidelines or schedule will result in the discontinuation of your visit.\n\nPlease reply “I agree” to this message in order to confirm the following:\n\n\"I agree that I have understood and that I am willing to follow all the guidelines presented above during my stay. I also understand that violation of any of the ashram guidelines and policies may lead to the discontinuation of my stay and I will have to depart from the Sadhguru Sannidhi premises.\"\n\nWe appreciate your attention to these guidelines, as they contribute to an enriching experience for all visitors.\n\nPranam \nVCD Applications\nSadhguru Sannidhi Bengaluru"}},"messageTimestamp":"1788518926","status":"PENDING"}}
